.TH imify-auth-login 1 "" "imify" ""
.SH NAME
imify\-auth\-login \- Sign in through the browser and store the login for the host
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimify auth login\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-browser\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-url\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign in through the browser and store the login for the API host.
.PP
Opens the browser and waits up to 5 minutes. The login is stored in the OS keychain, or in a file readable only by the user when no keychain is available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Write JSON instead of text [env: IMIFY_OUTPUT=json]
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-browser\fR
Print the sign\-in URL and read the redirect URL from the terminal instead of opening a browser
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Write the result only
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log more detail to stderr: \-v for debug, \-vv for trace
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm without prompting
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable color [env: NO_COLOR]
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
API host [env: IMIFY_API_URL] [default: config file, then https://platform.imify.ai]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  imify auth login
  imify auth login \-\-api\-url https://api.example.com
  imify auth login \-\-no\-browser
